{
  // Output filename and BoardLoader data-variable name:
  //   boardName "RP2040" -> designer/boards/RP2040/RP2040.json -> const RP2040Data = {...}
  "boardName": "RP2040",

  // Fallback human-readable name shown in the designer UI.  Overridden
  // by the matching `<id>.name=` entry in a sibling-or-ancestor
  // boards.txt when one is present (matched via `<id>.build.variant=`
  // against this variant's directory name) — for this board that's
  // "Waveshare RP2040 LCD 0.96" (variants/rp2040/boards.txt).
  "displayName": "Raspberry Pi Pico (RP2040)",

  // Same parser dialect as every other RP2040 board — see
  // ../board.json for the full rationale.
  "family": "rp2040",

  // No genuinely bidirectional-but-input-only pins on this board — the
  // onboard-LCD-dedicated GPIOs below are handled entirely via the
  // chipGpios capability overrides (empty capability sets), not via
  // inputOnlyGpios.
  "inputOnlyGpios": [],

  // Default transports — Serial only. Plain (non-WiFi) "rp2040" chip
  // bucket; this module has no onboard WiFi radio.
  "connections": ["serial"],

  "pinNotes": {},

  // pfodWeb NOTE (dedicated-hardware pin-exclusion audit, 2026-07-13):
  //
  // Board: Waveshare "RP2040-LCD-0.96" — a Pico-form-factor RP2040 board
  // with an onboard 0.96" 160x80 65K-colour IPS TFT LCD (ST7735S-family
  // controller, 4-wire SPI + separate D/C line), USB-C connector, and a
  // TPS63000 buck-boost DC-DC chip. No onboard user buttons and no
  // onboard NeoPixel/WS2812 — confirmed absent (see sources below);
  // GPIO25 drives the LCD's PWM-dimmable backlight, not a general-purpose
  // status LED.
  //
  // Sources consulted:
  // 1. This board's own pins_arduino.h (vendor-sourced comments already
  //    present, citing waveshare.com/wiki/RP2040-LCD-0.96 and the board's
  //    PDF/photo) — declares PIN_LCD_DC=8, PIN_LCD_CS=9, PIN_LCD_SCLK=10,
  //    PIN_LCD_MOSI=11, PIN_LCD_RST=12, PIN_LCD_BL=25 (`LDC_SPI (1u)`
  //    identifying the LCD as using the SPI1 peripheral, remapped in
  //    software to SCK=GPIO10/TX=GPIO11 rather than that peripheral's
  //    silicon-default SCK/TX pins GPIO14/15 — RP2040's GPIO function mux
  //    allows SPI1 SCK on GPIO10/14/26 and SPI1 TX on GPIO11/15/27, so
  //    this is a valid, ordinary remap, not a discrepancy).
  // 2. github.com/richteel/Waveshare-RP2040-LCD-0.96 (CircuitPython
  //    sample code for this exact board) — independently confirms the
  //    identical pin map: "GP8 - LCD_DC", "GP9 - LCD_CS", "GP10 -
  //    LCD_CLK", "GP11 - LCD_DIN", "GP12 - LCD_RST", "GP25 - LCD_BL". No
  //    button, LED, or NeoPixel GPIO definitions present anywhere in that
  //    repo.
  // 3. waveshare.com/wiki/RP2040-LCD-0.96 (official wiki, fetched via a
  //    text-extraction proxy since direct WebFetch returned HTTP 403) —
  //    feature list: "26 x multi-function GPIO pins", "2 x SPI, 2 x I2C,
  //    2 x UART, 3 x 12-bit ADC, 16 x controllable PWM channels",
  //    "0.96-inch 160x80 pixels 65K colorful IPS LCD display", USB-C,
  //    8 x PIO state machines, Li-po charge/discharge header, onboard
  //    DC-DC. The wiki's WS2812 demo code targets an *external* LED
  //    wired to a GPIO by the user (StateMachine sideset_base=Pin(0) in
  //    the demo) — confirmed NOT an onboard NeoPixel. No push-button of
  //    any kind is listed among the board's features or components.
  // 4. forums.raspberrypi.com/viewtopic.php?t=324715 — independent forum
  //    thread on this exact board; confirms pinout is "compatible with
  //    Raspberry Pi Pico" (shields reusable), confirms the ST7735S 4-wire
  //    SPI + D/C interface, confirms GPIO25 is the PWM-driven backlight
  //    pin (resolving an early doc/demo-code mismatch that briefly showed
  //    GPIO13 in some sample code — the schematic/GPIO25 wiring is what's
  //    physically correct), and flags an unrelated silkscreen SWDIO/
  //    SWDCLK swap (not a GPIO/capability issue, no action needed here).
  //    No button or onboard-LED mention anywhere in the thread.
  // 5. Standard RP2040 BOOTSEL: as with every other Pico-family board in
  //    this repo (rpipico, wiznet_5500_evb_pico, bridgetek_idm2040_43a),
  //    BOOTSEL is not a normal GPIO (arduino-pico exposes it as a
  //    `BOOTSEL` boolean, not `digitalRead()`), so it is out of scope for
  //    GPIO capability tagging, not a missed button.
  //
  // GPIO8/GPIO9 bus-role collision fix (separate bug class from the
  // pins_arduino.h vendor default, not from Waveshare's hardware): this
  // board's pins_arduino.h declared `PIN_WIRE0_SDA (8u)` / `PIN_WIRE0_SCL
  // (9u)` (Wire0's *default* I2C0 location on a stock Pico) plus a
  // top-level `static const uint8_t SDA = PIN_WIRE0_SDA;` / `SCL =
  // PIN_WIRE0_SCL;` alias — but GPIO8/9 on *this* board are physically
  // the LCD's dedicated DC/CS lines, so Wire0 can never actually be used
  // there. Because build_boards.js's i2c_sda/i2c_scl bus-role auto-append
  // keys off the SDA/SCL alias value unconditionally (fires even under a
  // chipGpios capabilities:[] override), GPIO8/9 would otherwise still be
  // mistagged i2c_sda/i2c_scl on top of full generic digital I/O. Fixed
  // at the source: removed `#define PIN_WIRE0_SDA/SCL` and the two
  // referencing `static const uint8_t SDA/SCL` lines from this board's
  // pins_arduino.h (Wire1 on GPIO6/7, unaffected, is untouched). This
  // pins_arduino.h copy is this repo's Designer-parsing mirror (already
  // diverged from the vendor's original, which still `#include
  // "../generic/common.h"` — see rp2040_board_variants/variants/
  // waveshare_rp2040_lcd_0_96/pins_arduino.h for the pristine original),
  // not a file compiled by the real arduino-pico toolchain, so this edit
  // does not affect real firmware builds.
  //
  // GPIO10/11/12/13/14/15/25: this board's pins_arduino.h already omits
  // any `static const uint8_t D10`..`D15`/`D25` alias (done in an earlier
  // audit pass, inline-commented "GPIO8,9,10,11,12,13,14,15,25 are
  // dedicated to an onboard peripheral"), so build_boards.js's
  // alias-driven parser already excludes GPIO10-15 and GPIO25 from the
  // Designer without any chipGpios entry. GPIO10/11/12/25 are confirmed
  // LCD-dedicated (SCLK/MOSI/RST/BL per sources #1-#2) and are documented
  // below anyway, matching this repo's bridgetek_idm2040_43a precedent of
  // recording dedicated-hardware pins even when already invisible.
  // GPIO13/14/15 (SPI1's *silicon-default* SS/SCK/MOSI pins, left unused
  // because the LCD remaps SPI1's SCK/MOSI to GPIO10/11 instead — see
  // source #1 reasoning above) are NOT confirmed by any source as
  // physically wired to the LCD or any other onboard peripheral; per this
  // audit's "confirm via real vendor documentation, never guess" rule
  // they are left out of chipGpios (no board.json entry needed since
  // they're already excluded from the Designer by the missing alias, and
  // no evidence supports either re-including or explicitly excluding them
  // as dedicated-hardware pins).
  //
  // Full findings/sources trail:
  // boardsDetails/rp2040/rp2040/waveshare_rp2040_lcd_0_96/notes.txt
  "chipGpios": {
    "8":  { "capabilities": [], "note": "PIN_LCD_DC — onboard 0.96in ST7735S-family LCD's dedicated SPI data/command select line. Not general-purpose. (Also the vendor's default Wire0 SDA pin, removed from this board's pins_arduino.h — see pfodWeb NOTE above.)" },
    "9":  { "capabilities": [], "note": "PIN_LCD_CS — onboard LCD's dedicated SPI1 chip-select line. Not general-purpose. (Also the vendor's default Wire0 SCL pin, removed from this board's pins_arduino.h — see pfodWeb NOTE above.)" },
    "10": { "capabilities": [], "note": "PIN_LCD_SCLK — onboard LCD's dedicated SPI1 clock line (remapped from SPI1's silicon-default GPIO14 in software). Not general-purpose. No pins_arduino.h alias declared for this GPIO (documented here for clarity only)." },
    "11": { "capabilities": [], "note": "PIN_LCD_MOSI (DIN) — onboard LCD's dedicated SPI1 data-out line (remapped from SPI1's silicon-default GPIO15 in software). Not general-purpose. No pins_arduino.h alias declared for this GPIO (documented here for clarity only)." },
    "12": { "capabilities": [], "note": "PIN_LCD_RST — onboard LCD's dedicated hardware reset line. Not general-purpose. No pins_arduino.h alias declared for this GPIO (documented here for clarity only)." },
    "25": { "capabilities": [], "note": "PIN_LCD_BL — onboard LCD's dedicated, PWM-dimmable backlight-enable line (confirmed via richteel sample code and Raspberry Pi forum thread t=324715). Not a general-purpose status LED and not a spare PWM output — entirely committed to the onboard display. No pins_arduino.h alias declared for this GPIO (documented here for clarity only)." }
  },

  // Same 8-bit analogWrite() default as every other RP2040/RP2350 board.
  "pwm": { "min": 0, "max": 255, "method": "analogWrite" },

  // No hardware DAC on RP2040/RP2350.
  "dac": {},

  // RP2040's one 12-bit ADC (0-4095), ~3.3V reference — same as every
  // other RP2040 board. Not affected by this audit (none of the excluded
  // GPIOs carry an analog_input alias in the first place).
  "adc": { "bits": 12, "max": 4095, "defaultRefVolts": "3.3" }
}
